WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.100
Henry Cavill may be making a return to a high-profile
franchise.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.320
No, not that one.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.500
The rumor-mongerers at We Got This Covered
are back with a new report that's too good

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.250
to believe, claiming that Henry Cavill, who
portrayed the villainous CIA turncoat August

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.380
Walker in Mission: Impossible Fallout, may
return for the next installment.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.340
You may be wondering how this is possible.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.980
Fans will remember that during Fallout's climax,
Ethan Hunt was forced to chased down Walker

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.180
in a commandeered helicopter in order to prevent
the latter from putting into motion a plan

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.180
to contaminate a massive portion of the world's
water supply with stolen nuclear weapons.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:39.060
After a stunningly shot, Cruise-endangering
aerial chase, Hunt forces Walker to crash-land

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.780
by... well, just straight-up crashing into
him, then engages the villain in fisticuffs

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.890
on a treacherous, snowy mountainside.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.640
Of course, the ever-resourceful Hunt finds
an exceedingly cinematic way to dispatch his

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.360
nemesis, dropping one of the helicopters'
winch hooks on him and crushing him to death.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.320
The detonators are secured, the world's water
supply is safe, and as for Walker well, he's

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.480
just super-dead.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.000
If you're thinking it seems like Fallout's
ending would preclude a return to the role

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.830
of Walker by Cavill, well, we're right there
with you.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.040
So, how would it happen?

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.020
A dream sequence?

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.020
Perhaps a flashback?

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.740
Maybe the as-yet untitled Mission: Impossible
7 will be a prequel?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.250
Or perhaps August Walker was actually the
nefarious alter-ego of Superman, a guy whom

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.530
he bears a suspicious resemblance to, and
he was therefore able to simply shake off

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.460
getting a half-ton winch hook dropped on him?

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.390
In our humble opinion, the answer is none
of the above, because we're pretty sure that

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:31.390
this rumor is baloney for a couple of simple
reasons.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.200
First: Cavill's character is, again, dead
as a doornail at the conclusion of Fallout.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.950
Second: the mysterious "inside sources" are
literally the only ones reporting this, and

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.610
those sources sources that may well just be
"Reddit posts and Twitter" are often terribly,

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:46.800
embarrassingly wrong.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.180
Sorry, but it's true.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.300
"People actually fall for that."

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.200
Also, there's the fact that when it comes
to Mission: Impossible 7 and 8, which will

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.420
shoot back to back, very few details have
been made public.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:02.799
We suppose it's possible that a hit-and-miss,
generally unreliable source could luck its

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:07.230
way into accurate information that exactly
zero reputable media outlets have yet caught

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:07.760
a whiff of.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.520
But do we have any reason to believe it?

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:10.840
No, not really.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:15.671
No, we're going to go ahead and peg this rumor
as "completely unfounded" and "probably total

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.180
bunk."

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.180
First and foremost, we are of the opinion
that Hayley Atwell improves anything she is

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:24.510
involved with, and the next two Mission: Impossible
movies will have precisely one more Hayley

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.620
Atwell than any of the previous films in the
franchise have had.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.780
Star of the Marvel Cinematic Universe and
the late, great series Agent Carter, Atwell

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.180
is one of the more talented actresses working
today and she's already proven that she totally

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.960
has what it takes to be an action star.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.860
Second, the ageless, apparently indestructible
Cruise is returning as Hunt, as is Rebecca

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.190
Ferguson, who has shined in the last three
Mission: Impossible pictures as Ilsa Faust,

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:51.280
the former British intelligence agent and
operative for the criminal organization known

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.060
as the Syndicate who is now firmly on the
side of Hunt and the IMF.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.810
Her chemistry with Cruise has only grown more
potent during her tenure in the franchise,

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.680
and her return is most welcome.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.880
Finally, writer/director Christopher McQuarrie
will be back to fill both roles on Mission:

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.230
Impossible 7 and 8, and this is a guy who
knows how to write for and direct Cruise perhaps

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.740
better than anyone in Hollywood.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:16.080
He wrote and helmed 2012's Jack Reacher, turned
in an amazing screenplay for the time-twisting,

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.569
sci-fi Edge of Tomorrow, and has masterminded
the previous two Mission: Impossible movies,

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:22.110
which were among the series' best.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:26.430
Yes, he also wrote The Mummy, the film that
both launched and sealed the doom of Universal's

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.120
Dark Universe franchise, but we can forgive
him for that.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.360
Mission: Impossible has improbably proven
to be one of the best action franchises of

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.360
all time, starting off strong and seeming
to only get better as it keeps trucking along.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.370
Personally, we can't wait for the seventh
and eighth installments to hit screens, and

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.810
when they do, we're pretty sure it'll be without
Cavill.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:47.870
Cruise, though, seems to want to keep making
these movies until he's 80 and we have a feeling

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.240
he probably will, provided one of them doesn't
finally do him in.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.840
Mission: Impossible 7 is slated for release
on July 23, 2021; Mission: Impossible 8 will

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.300
follow on August 5, 2022.

